# React Patterns

> Extends the common and TypeScript rules for the Vite React SPA.

## Components and Routing

- Write function components and hooks. Do not add class components except a
  narrowly required error-boundary implementation.
- React Router owns navigation and route composition. Keep filter and sort
  state in validated URL search parameters so useful views are shareable.
- Route modules coordinate data and feature surfaces; reusable UI stays inside
  focused feature or component modules.
- Use stable list and grid row identifiers. Never use an array index where
  ordering or membership can change.

## State Ownership

- Local interaction state stays local.
- Apollo Client owns bounded GraphQL pages, facets, aggregates, dataset
  metadata, export status, and detail.
- URL parameters own shareable filter and sort state.
- React Context plus versioned local storage owns low-frequency preferences.
  Validate stored values and recover safely to defaults.
- Query results stay in the Apollo cache as bounded cursor pages, facets, and
  aggregates served by ClickHouse; do not accumulate the full corpus in React
  state or Zustand, and do not introduce Redux. Zustand holds live connection
  state (`connection`, `lastEventId`, `pendingUpdates`, and a bounded recent
  Finding-event list) only.

## Data and Rendering

- Do not fetch GraphQL control-plane data in ad hoc effects. Use Apollo Client
  with explicit loading/error/empty states.
- Keep filtering, sorting, suggestions, pagination, and export out of render:
  express them as GraphQL arguments (`filters`, `sort`, `search`, `timeRange`,
  `analysisMode`, `after`, `first`) or an export mutation and let ClickHouse
  do the work. Apply SSE `DatasetEvent`s through the Apollo cache or a bounded
  refetch, never by re-sorting loaded rows in a component.
- Memoize only when identity is contractually important or profiling shows a
  real cost.
- Compose shadcn components semantically. Use TanStack Table + Virtual and
  Recharts via shadcn charts as the grid and chart stack.

## Accessibility

Use semantic structure, labels, keyboard support, visible focus, meaningful
chart alternatives, and announced loading/error states. Grid and chart
integration must remain usable without pointer-only interaction.
